SINA_SMART["histo1-urinary"] = {"lecture":"histo1-urinary","title":"Histology of the urinary system","mapStatus":"auto: generated by universal.py from the lecture summary and key points; not human-reviewed","los":[{"id":"histo1-urinary:e0","text":"Kidney: filtration, fluid and BP (renin), erythropoietin, reabsorption.","topic":"Functions and organisation","sec":0,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"histo1-urinary:e1","text":"Uriniferous tubule = nephron + collecting duct; nephron = corpuscle + tubule.","topic":"Functions and organisation","sec":0,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"histo1-urinary:e2","text":"Cortical nephrons 80-85%; juxtamedullary 15-20% with long loops.","topic":"Functions and organisation","sec":0,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"histo1-urinary:e3","text":"Bowman's capsule: parietal simple squamous, visceral podocytes.","topic":"The renal corpuscle and filtration barrier","sec":1,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"histo1-urinary:e4","text":"Filtration barrier: fenestrated endothelium + GBM (type IV collagen; charge barrier) + podocyte slits.","topic":"The renal corpuscle and filtration barrier","sec":1,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"histo1-urinary:e5","text":"Mesangial cells: support, contract (angiotensin II), clear immune complexes.","topic":"The renal corpuscle and filtration barrier","sec":1,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"histo1-urinary:e6","text":"PCT: acidophilic, brush border; DCT: no brush border, aldosterone.","topic":"Tubules and the juxtaglomerular apparatus","sec":2,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"histo1-urinary:e7","text":"Thin descending limb permeable to water; ascending not.","topic":"Tubules and the juxtaglomerular apparatus","sec":2,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"histo1-urinary:e8","text":"Collecting duct: principal (Na⁺, water) and intercalated (H⁺, HCO₃⁻) cells.","topic":"Tubules and the juxtaglomerular apparatus","sec":2,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"histo1-urinary:e9","text":"JGA: macula densa + renin-secreting JG cells + extraglomerular mesangium.","topic":"Tubules and the juxtaglomerular apparatus","sec":2,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"histo1-urinary:e10","text":"Urothelium: dome cells, plaques; ureter inner longitudinal + middle circular muscle.","topic":"Excretory passages","sec":3,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"}],"vmap":{},"mlevel":{"18pj5s5":"a","1jr99ij":"a","1361fet":"a","1x30h1v":"a","b6tms8":"a","1e874cg":"a","1hgwxpj":"a","qez942":"a","j4obou":"a","8jhn68":"a","i102lu":"a","v2xayn":"a","g319h2":"a","1p224t4":"a","16llga6":"a"},"mapCounts":{"verified":0,"auto":15,"ambiguous":0,"missing":0},"mrules":[],"items":[],"experimental":[],"status":{},"difficulty":{},"expl":{"histo1-urinary:e0":{"s":0,"u":["Kidney: filtration, fluid and BP (renin), erythropoietin, reabsorption.","The urinary system (1) filters and excretes, (2) balances body fluid, regulates blood pressure through renin and acts as an endocrine gland making erythropoietin , and (3) maintains homeostasis by reabsorbing small molecules (amino acids, glucose), ions (Na⁺, Ca²⁺, Cl⁻) and water."],"dp":[]},"histo1-urinary:e1":{"s":0,"u":["Uriniferous tubule = nephron + collecting duct; nephron = corpuscle + tubule.","The uriniferous tubule = nephron + collecting duct; the nephron = renal corpuscle + renal tubule (PCT, loop of Henle, DCT).","Cortical nephrons (80-85%) have corpuscles in the outer cortex and short loops; juxtamedullary nephrons (15-20%) sit near the medulla with long loops reaching deep into it, allowing concentrated or dilute urine."],"dp":[]},"histo1-urinary:e2":{"s":0,"u":["Cortical nephrons 80-85%; juxtamedullary 15-20% with long loops.","Cortical nephrons (80-85%) have corpuscles in the outer cortex and short loops; juxtamedullary nephrons (15-20%) sit near the medulla with long loops reaching deep into it, allowing concentrated or dilute urine.","The uriniferous tubule = nephron + collecting duct; the nephron = renal corpuscle + renal tubule (PCT, loop of Henle, DCT)."],"dp":[]},"histo1-urinary:e3":{"s":1,"u":["Bowman's capsule: parietal simple squamous, visceral podocytes.","The parietal layer is simple squamous epithelium, becoming cuboidal at the urinary pole where it continues into the PCT; the visceral layer is made of podocytes .","The corpuscle is the glomerulus inside Bowman's capsule ."],"dp":[]},"histo1-urinary:e4":{"s":1,"u":["Filtration barrier: fenestrated endothelium + GBM (type IV collagen; charge barrier) + podocyte slits.","The filtration barrier has three parts: fenestrated endothelium ; the glomerular basement membrane , a lamina densa (type IV collagen, laminin: size filter) between two laminae rarae (heparan sulphate, fibronectin: charge barrier restricting anionic molecules); and the podocytes , whose primary processes give secondary processes ( pedicels ) that interdigitate on the basement membrane, leaving filtration slits bridged by a diaphragm."],"dp":[{"h":"Protein in the urine: which layer failed?","t":"Albumin is small enough to pass the pores of the endothelium but is kept out by the negative charge of the basement membrane and by the slit diaphragms between podocyte pedicels. In nephrotic syndrome the podocytes' foot processes flatten and fuse (effacement) and the slit diaphragms are lost, so large amounts of protein leak into the urine, the plasma albumin falls and oedema follows. In minimal change disease the light microscope looks normal: only electron microscopy shows the effaced pedicels, a direct use of the ultrastructure in this lecture. Source: the lecture's filtration barrier; standard renal pathology."}]},"histo1-urinary:e5":{"s":1,"u":["Mesangial cells: support, contract (angiotensin II), clear immune complexes.","Mesangial cells support the capillaries, are contractile with angiotensin II receptors (reducing flow) and natriuretic factor receptors, make matrix, clear immune complexes trapped by the basement membrane and produce cytokines and prostaglandins; at the vascular pole they are extraglomerular mesangial cells .","Podocytes contain actin and can contract."],"dp":[]},"histo1-urinary:e6":{"s":2,"u":["PCT: acidophilic, brush border; DCT: no brush border, aldosterone.","DCT : shorter cuboidal cells, no brush border ; with aldosterone it reabsorbs Na⁺ and secretes K⁺.","PCT : cuboidal cells, acidophilic cytoplasm (many mitochondria), lysosomes and vesicles, a brush border of microvilli; surrounded by peritubular capillaries."],"dp":[]},"histo1-urinary:e7":{"s":2,"u":["Thin descending limb permeable to water; ascending not.","Loop of Henle : thick segments lined by low cuboidal cells, thin segments by squamous epithelium; the thin descending limb is permeable to water , the ascending limb is not."],"dp":[]},"histo1-urinary:e8":{"s":2,"u":["Collecting duct: principal (Na⁺, water) and intercalated (H⁺, HCO₃⁻) cells.","Collecting duct : widens towards the papilla (area cribrosa); principal cells (basal infoldings, a primary cilium as mechanosensor; absorb Na⁺ and water, secrete K⁺) and intercalated cells (microvilli; secrete H⁺ or HCO₃⁻)."],"dp":[]},"histo1-urinary:e9":{"s":2,"u":["JGA: macula densa + renin-secreting JG cells + extraglomerular mesangium.","The juxtaglomerular apparatus : the macula densa , tall, closely packed DCT cells with apical nuclei next to the arterioles, senses the ionic content and volume of the tubular fluid and signals the juxtaglomerular cells , modified smooth muscle of the afferent (sometimes efferent) arteriole with renin granules; with the extraglomerular mesangial cells."],"dp":[]},"histo1-urinary:e10":{"s":3,"u":["Urothelium: dome cells, plaques; ureter inner longitudinal + middle circular muscle.","Ureter : mucosa, muscular coat of inner longitudinal and middle circular layers, with an outer longitudinal layer only at the distal end, and fibrous adventitia; the oblique entry into the bladder compresses the ureter when the bladder fills, limiting reflux.","Transitional epithelium (urothelium) lines them up to the first part of the male urethra: impermeable to water and salts, 2 layers in the calyces, 4-5 in the ureter, more in the bladder; dome-shaped surface cells whose apical membrane has rigid plaques that fold and unfold with volume."],"dp":[]}},"meta":{"18pj5s5":{"a":"recall","vg":"histo1-urinary:e2/recall/1"},"1jr99ij":{"a":"recall","vg":"histo1-urinary:e3/recall/1"},"1361fet":{"a":"recall","vg":"histo1-urinary:e3/recall/2"},"1x30h1v":{"a":"relationship","vg":"histo1-urinary:e4/relationship/1"},"b6tms8":{"a":"relationship","vg":"histo1-urinary:e4/relationship/2"},"1e874cg":{"a":"recall","vg":"histo1-urinary:e5/recall/1"},"1hgwxpj":{"a":"recall","vg":"histo1-urinary:e6/recall/1"},"qez942":{"a":"recall","vg":"histo1-urinary:e7/recall/1"},"j4obou":{"a":"recall","vg":"histo1-urinary:e6/recall/2"},"8jhn68":{"a":"recall","vg":"histo1-urinary:e9/recall/1"},"i102lu":{"a":"recall","vg":"histo1-urinary:e9/recall/2"},"v2xayn":{"a":"recall","vg":"histo1-urinary:e8/recall/1"},"g319h2":{"a":"recall","vg":"histo1-urinary:e10/recall/1"},"1p224t4":{"a":"recall","vg":"histo1-urinary:e10/recall/2"},"16llga6":{"a":"recall","vg":"histo1-urinary:e10/recall/3"}},"explRev":"6aff91e6ae3e"};
